X) × 1.7 (Y), bezel dark gray #2B2F33, screen fill pale blue #A8D8EE; a red baseline #D8342B runs horizontally across the lower third; peaks are thin vertical black/red lines rising from it — two short peaks (heights 0.25, 0.45) at 30% and 34% of screen width, one tall peak (0.95) at 72%, and a medium peak (0.6) at 78%; small oval stand base below. Labels: 'Sample in tube' at upper-left (x≈-3.4, y≈+2.6) with a thin black leader to the tube at y≈+1.9; 'Radiofrequency generator' at far left (x≈-5.8, y≈-1.1); 'Detector and amplifier' at (x≈+4.6, y≈-2.4). Resonance physics: ν = γB₀/2π; for ¹H, γ/2π = 42.58 MHz/T, so the fixed 9.56 MHz readout would resonate near B₀ ≈ 0.22 T — for the demo treat the slider range 1.0–2.6 T as the swept variable and place three resonance events at B₀ ≈ 1.38, 1.52, 2.15, 2.28 T mapped to the four screen peaks (same order left→right as the peak x-positions).",
